<div class='page-hero'><div><h1 class='hero-title'>12 · INTO — 动态穿越边界、猛烈碰撞、深入调查与形态转化<span class='hero-badge'>📖 EPE Ch.2 §4.2-4.3</span></h1><p class='hero-sub'>INTO: Dynamic Boundary-Crossing, Collision, Penetration & Transformation</p></div><div style='font-size:0.88em;color:#475569;font-weight:600;'>共 <b>41</b> 个独立义项 • <b>123</b> 句中英对照例句</div></div>
<details class='epe-book-drawer' open><summary class='epe-drawer-bar'><span>📚 《English Prepositions Explained》(Seth Lindstromberg) 原著核心精讲 — Chapter 2 (§4.1–§4.3 IN vs INTO) & Chapter 4 (§4)</span><span style='font-size:0.84em;color:#6366f1;font-weight:600;'>点击收起 / 展开原书理论图式 ▾</span></summary><div class='epe-drawer-grid'><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>🧭 原著空间与功能核心图式 (Core Schema)</div><div><b>动态穿越边界进入 (→○)、猛烈冲击力与「状态/形态即容器」隐喻</b>：INTO 是 IN 的动态及物复合形式（必须接显性宾语，不能单独作不及物词尾，但被动或前置宾语如 <i>That needs looking into</i> 合法）。</div><div class='epe-box-title' style='margin-top:12px;'>📝 原书典型语料例句 (Authentic Examples from EPE)</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>The moment he walked in the door... vs He walked into the door and it broke.</i> [Ch.2 (17a-b)]</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>He broke into/*in our meeting/conversation. / That needs looking into.</i> [Ch.2 (12), (15)]</div></div><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>⚖️ 原书近义小品词深度辨析与隐喻机制 (Key Contrasts & Metaphors)</div><ul class='epe-contrast-list'><li><b>INTO vs IN 的三大铁律 (Ch.2 §4.2)</b>：① <b>动态与撞击</b>：<i>crash into a tree / walk into a door</i> 强调运动与猛烈接触；② <b>持续深入</b>：<i>drive deeper into/*in the forest</i> 表达向纵深穿透；③ <b>抽象宾语垄断</b>：当宾语是谈话、调查、思绪等抽象事物时，只能用 INTO（<i>break into our conversation; look into a complaint</i>）。</li><li><b>炼金术与青蛙变王子隐喻 (Ch.2 §4.3)</b>：在 <i>change/turn/make x into y</i> 及 <i>talk/coax sb into doing</i> 中，新的物理形态、黄金属性或行动决定被视为一个全新的容器空间。</li></ul></div></div></details>

